WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
In the hustle and bustle of building a business,

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.880
it can be easy to overlook certain inherent risks

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.480
that could shut you down for good.

4
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.140
As a business owner, it is easy to get caught up

5
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.240
in just being busy.

6
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.480
Who has time to think about risk mitigation,

7
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.460
tax planning strategies, business preservation techniques,

8
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.060
and business continuity issues?

9
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.820
It's important to stop and make sure

10
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.800
what you want to have happen does happen

11
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.000
if the worst thing that can happen happens.

12
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.840
For example, what would you do

13
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.840
if the most crucial person in your company,

14
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.120
other than yourself, had a major health issue

15
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.900
and couldn't come into work for several months?

16
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.800
What would happen if your business partner died

17
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.300
or just wanted to leave the business?

18
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.280
What would you do if your partner got divorced?

19
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.260
How would the company ownership be transferred?

20
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.640
When you're ready to retire,

21
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.700
are you planning to keep this business in the family,

22
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.420
sell it to a dedicated employee,

23
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.860
or sell it to a third party?

24
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.340
Are you taking full advantage

25
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.320
of how your business can help you save for retirement?

26
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.420
Have you even thought about your own retirement?

27
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.540
These are all questions you should have an answer for.

28
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.780
Educating yourself about the best practices

29
00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.300
when it comes to business preservation

30
00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.900
is absolutely critical.

31
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.920
You need to be up to speed on concepts

32
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.320
like buy-sell agreements, key person coverage,

33
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.180
risk transference, business succession plans,

34
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.280
planning for your own retirement, and more.

35
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.820
Every company is different

36
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.200
and there is no one-size-fits-all solution,

37
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.540
which makes a proper and personal analysis

38
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.360
key to minimizing unnecessary or excessive risk.

39
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:19.520
The great Benjamin Franklin once said,

40
00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.880
failure to plan is planning to fail,

41
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.400
and nowhere does this ring more true than in business.

42
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.940
Reach out to a business preservation specialist today

43
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.820
for a free educational consultation

44
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.420
on where your business' potential pain points are

45
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.380
and what can be done

46
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.440
to assure your business builds your wealth.

47
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.680
One short meeting can give you the knowledge you need

48
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.160
to properly protect what you've worked so hard to build.
